# Playwright and PR recordings

## Projects

| Project | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `chromium` / `mobile` | Phase 1 regression |
| `phase2` | Phase 2 behavioural e2e (`e2e/phase2/*.spec.ts` except happy-paths) |
| `phase2-recordings` | Named happy-path videos for PR review (`happy-paths.spec.ts`) |

## Every Phase 2 PR

1. Cover the new behaviour under `e2e/phase2/` (assert UI + sync outcomes).
2. Extend or keep `happy-paths.spec.ts` recordings current for the demo flow.
3. Run `npm run test:e2e:phase2` so CI can upload `e2e/artifacts/pr-videos/*.webm` + `manifest.json`.
4. Use stable `data-testid` hooks (`app-menu-trigger`, `auth-modal`, `continuation-prompt`, …).

## Recording conventions

- Serial happy-path suite; save via `savePhase2Video` / `saveContextVideo` in `e2e/phase2/helpers/cloud-utils.ts`.
- Name files `phase2-NN-short-slug.webm` and register them in `manifest.json` (`title` + `description`).
- Simulate devices with `setDeviceId` / `setDeviceDisplayName` and separate browser contexts — not two accounts.

## Helpers

Reuse `e2e/helpers/test-utils.ts` and `e2e/phase2/helpers/*`. Prefer fixtures under `e2e/fixtures/` over generating large PDFs in-test.

## ❌ / ✅

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — behaviour only verified manually; no artifact for the PR
await page.click('text=Sign in');

// ✅ GOOD — asserted e2e + named recording entry
await signInViaUi(page);
await savePhase2Video(page, 'phase2-01-app-menu-and-sign-in');
recordings.push({ file: '...', title: '...', description: '...' });
```
